\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
(1) Play/Pause:
\series default
 Starts or stops a simulation: the repeated, time based invocation of the run method of a compiled Java class (a class which extends the class Model). The menu of the action contains 
\series bold
Set Time Interval
\series default
 (the interval of the invocation) and 
\series bold
Counter Reset
\series default
 (sets the time steps of the status line to 0).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
(2) Setup:
\series default
 Invokes the setup method of the compiled Java class (if available).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
(3) R:
\series default
 Starts R with an Rserve connection (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:The-R-Perspective"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

). The menu of the action contains 
\series bold
Start Rserve/Stop Rserve (within R)
\series default
, 
\series bold
Terminate R
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Kill All R Processes
\series default
 (if necessary).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
(4) Create Projects or Files:
\series default
 Creates a project with a default file in one step: a Bio7 Java project (also with a WindowBuilder GUI, OpenGL, WorldWind or an ImageJ plugin), a project with an R, R Markdown, R Shiny, Python, Jython, Groovy, JavaScript, ImageJ macro or LaTeX file, a reproducible project or another project or file (
\series bold
Other...
\series default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
(5) Editor actions:
\series default
 The actions of the active editor, e.g., 
\series bold
Interpret R
\series default
 for the R editor, the compilation of Java code for the Java editor or 
\series bold
Interpret ImageJ Macro
\series default
 for the ImageJ macro editor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
(6) Open a Terminal:
\series default
 Opens a terminal (a shell of the operating system) in the Terminal view.
\end_layout

